WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.136 --> 00:00:05.208
- The completion of the
task is really important

00:00:05.208 --> 00:00:07.515
to release the chemicals,
to feel like a winner,

00:00:07.515 --> 00:00:09.175
to feel like you've got
that off your plate.

00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:11.256
I wonder how you break
it down for when you're

00:00:11.256 --> 00:00:12.501
working on the bigger projects.

00:00:12.501 --> 00:00:14.096
Say you're working on a book.

00:00:14.096 --> 00:00:15.472
You've done 80 plus.

00:00:15.472 --> 00:00:18.113
You're an expert on
writing best selling books.

00:00:18.113 --> 00:00:20.553
So a part of your most important thing is

00:00:20.553 --> 00:00:21.702
hey, I'm on a book deadline.

00:00:21.702 --> 00:00:23.192
I need to get this done.

00:00:23.192 --> 00:00:25.440
Obviously, you won't be
able to write an entire book

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:26.983
in the first two hours of a day.

00:00:26.983 --> 00:00:29.184
So how would you chunk it down so that

00:00:29.184 --> 00:00:30.384
you get that feeling?

00:00:30.384 --> 00:00:32.416
You want to leave feeling like
you accomplished something.

00:00:32.416 --> 00:00:34.734
That you got something,
that you checked the box.

00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:37.022
How would you break down a
bigger goal for the morning?

00:00:37.022 --> 00:00:40.432
- I'm assuming that everybody
who is watching this

00:00:40.432 --> 00:00:43.081
wants to become rich sooner or later.

00:00:43.081 --> 00:00:44.920
And sooner is preferable.

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:45.753
Alright?

00:00:45.753 --> 00:00:48.150
The way that you become
rich is you deliver results

00:00:48.150 --> 00:00:49.867
that people will pay you for.

00:00:49.867 --> 00:00:53.089
Well, one of the greatest
result tools in the world

00:00:53.089 --> 00:00:54.785
is called a checklist.

00:00:54.785 --> 00:00:56.224
And a checklist is very simply a

00:00:56.224 --> 00:00:58.535
list of every step in the process from

00:00:58.535 --> 00:01:00.360
step one to step two to step three.

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:02.782
Very much like a recipe that is organized.

00:01:02.782 --> 00:01:06.461
That says this is what you do
to prepare a particular dish.

00:01:06.461 --> 00:01:08.302
You do these things
and you do these things

00:01:08.302 --> 00:01:09.562
and you bring out these things

00:01:09.562 --> 00:01:12.162
and you take these
ingredients in this order

00:01:12.162 --> 00:01:15.045
in this quantity and so on.

00:01:15.045 --> 00:01:16.812
And you put it all together.

00:01:16.812 --> 00:01:19.509
So, some years ago, I did something

00:01:19.509 --> 00:01:20.716
which was really quite ridiculous.

00:01:20.716 --> 00:01:24.165
I wrote a book and I
promoted the heck out it.

00:01:24.165 --> 00:01:26.668
It cost me more to promote the book than

00:01:26.668 --> 00:01:29.420
I got from royalties or advances.

00:01:29.420 --> 00:01:32.014
And then after three
months, they told me that we

00:01:32.014 --> 00:01:34.452
have no more interest
in promoting your book.

00:01:34.452 --> 00:01:35.892
And I said, well why?

00:01:35.892 --> 00:01:38.567
I mean we're doing so well,
interviews, blah blah blah.

00:01:38.567 --> 00:01:41.907
They said, well after three
months, the window closes.

00:01:41.907 --> 00:01:43.707
Because when you write a book,
there's a three month window

00:01:43.707 --> 00:01:45.660
prior to the book coming out.

00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:47.972
And three months after
it comes out it closes

00:01:47.972 --> 00:01:49.796
and we go onto other books.

00:01:49.796 --> 00:01:52.275
Your book is now an old story.

00:01:52.275 --> 00:01:54.025
It's yesterdays news.

00:01:55.084 --> 00:01:57.435
And I said, well geez,
what can I do with that?

00:01:57.435 --> 00:02:00.807
I said, I know, I'll write
book every three months.

00:02:00.807 --> 00:02:02.149
And I made that decision.

00:02:02.149 --> 00:02:06.640
I'm just now working today
to finish my 82nd book.

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:07.473
- Wow.

00:02:07.473 --> 00:02:08.719
- It will be finished by Friday.

00:02:08.719 --> 00:02:10.781
And with all the major publishers.

00:02:10.781 --> 00:02:12.877
Every one is published
by major publishers.

00:02:12.877 --> 00:02:14.183
No self publishing.

00:02:14.183 --> 00:02:15.901
And I am talking about Simon and Schuster,

00:02:15.901 --> 00:02:19.184
and Wylie, and I have
just published four books

00:02:19.184 --> 00:02:21.741
with biggest publisher in the
world, Penguin Random House.

00:02:21.741 --> 00:02:23.567
And they came to me
and asked for the book.

00:02:23.567 --> 00:02:24.983
So a person says, how do you write a book?

00:02:24.983 --> 00:02:27.430
I say, I take out my checklist, and I say,

00:02:27.430 --> 00:02:29.448
the first thing I need to know.

00:02:29.448 --> 00:02:32.045
We need to agree on the subject, alright?

00:02:32.045 --> 00:02:34.013
And I only write on a
subject that I have put in

00:02:34.013 --> 00:02:36.407
hundreds of hours of
research and experience.

00:02:36.407 --> 00:02:38.887
The second thing we need to know is when

00:02:38.887 --> 00:02:40.408
is the drop dead date?

00:02:40.408 --> 00:02:42.999
When do you plan to publish
the book, release the book?

00:02:42.999 --> 00:02:44.465
And when do you have to
have it in your hands?

00:02:44.465 --> 00:02:48.368
Which is usually fully
six months before the book

00:02:48.368 --> 00:02:49.337
is published, okay?

00:02:49.337 --> 00:02:50.666
So I work back from there.

00:02:50.666 --> 00:02:51.863
And then I've got a checklist.

00:02:51.863 --> 00:02:54.469
Now I know what the
subject of the books is,

00:02:54.469 --> 00:02:56.896
when the book has to be in
the hands of the publishers,

00:02:56.896 --> 00:03:00.208
and then I work all the
way back to step one.

00:03:00.208 --> 00:03:02.393
And by the way, anybody who wants this,

00:03:02.393 --> 00:03:05.110
just go onto my website BrianTracy.com,

00:03:05.110 --> 00:03:07.774
and just say Brian's
checklist for writing.

00:03:07.774 --> 00:03:08.696
It's free.

00:03:08.696 --> 00:03:09.615
And it's 20 points.

00:03:09.615 --> 00:03:11.929
Cause people kept asking me,
how do you write so many books?

00:03:11.929 --> 00:03:14.379
I've written now four or five books a year

00:03:14.379 --> 00:03:15.796
for twenty years.

00:03:17.834 --> 00:03:21.722
And now I say, well I'm
out of it now, I'm done.

00:03:21.722 --> 00:03:24.243
This last two months
I've gotten requests for

00:03:24.243 --> 00:03:25.910
five books for 2017.

00:03:26.819 --> 00:03:28.272
From this publisher and that publisher and

00:03:28.272 --> 00:03:30.698
one other publisher wants two and

00:03:30.698 --> 00:03:33.762
I said, geez, I said, you
know, I got to take a break.

00:03:33.762 --> 00:03:35.882
No, we want the books
because these books sell.

00:03:35.882 --> 00:03:38.402
They just kind of tumble over each other.

00:03:38.402 --> 00:03:40.056
One sells and the second sells and

00:03:40.056 --> 00:03:42.337
I said, so here's the formula.

00:03:42.337 --> 00:03:44.770
Just simply download the
formula like a recipe

00:03:44.770 --> 00:03:45.896
and follow the formula.

00:03:45.896 --> 00:03:50.011
It takes tremendous
discipline to write a book.

00:03:50.011 --> 00:03:51.416
You can appreciate this because
you've written your book.

00:03:51.416 --> 00:03:53.616
I said, writing a book is like

00:03:53.616 --> 00:03:55.985
digging a ditch to the horizon.

00:03:55.985 --> 00:03:57.284
- (laughs)

00:03:57.284 --> 00:03:58.690
- Can you picture that?

00:03:58.690 --> 00:03:59.523
- Yeah.

00:03:59.523 --> 00:04:02.019
- In other words, you just work and work

00:04:02.019 --> 00:04:03.698
and you lift up your head and

00:04:03.698 --> 00:04:05.474
all you can see is the horizon.

00:04:05.474 --> 00:04:07.988
You put your head down and
work and work and work.

00:04:07.988 --> 00:04:10.497
You look up and it's still
the horizon out there.

00:04:10.497 --> 00:04:13.208
Hour after hour after hour.

00:04:13.208 --> 00:04:15.244
But you've got to get started.

00:04:15.244 --> 00:04:16.714
- Well I'm going to
check out the checklist.

00:04:16.714 --> 00:04:18.610
It took me two years
to get this thing out,

00:04:18.610 --> 00:04:21.416
so I'm envious to get a new
book out every three months.

00:04:21.416 --> 00:04:24.853
Maybe, that list will help
me too for the next version.

00:04:24.853 --> 00:04:26.770
Thank you for the tips.

